\[
G_{i, \mu}^{\text {ang }}=2^{1-\zeta} \sum_{i, j, k}\left(1+\lambda \cos \theta_{i j k}\right)^{\zeta} \mathrm{e}^{-\eta\left(R_{i j}^{2}+R_{i k}^{2}\right)} f_{\mathrm{c}}\left(R_{i j}\right) f_{\mathrm{c}}\left(R_{i k}\right)
\]
can be used, which includes a larger number of angle terms by omitting the restriction of \(R_{j k}<R_{\mathrm{c}}\) as shown in Figure 10.

