\section*{Biography}

Jörg Behler graduated in chemistry at the Universität Dortmund in 2000. He then joined the theory department of the Fritz-HaberInstitute of the Max-Planck-Society in Berlin, where he received his Ph.D. in physics in 2004. After a postdoctoral stay at the same place he moved to the ETH Zurich in 2006. In 2007 he established an independent research group at the Ruhr-Universität Bochum funded by several grants including a Liebig fellowship, as well as the DFG Emmy Noether and Heisenberg programs. In 2014 he obtained his habilitation in theoretical chemistry. In 2017 he became a full professor for theoretical chemistry at the Georg-August-Universität Göttingen. His main research interest is the development of machine learning potentials with applications to complex systems in chemistry and materials science.

